{"domain": "gamma_window", "ev": "note", "source": "portage-depot/gamma_chart.py; GGV3 1406.0886 tex:1735-1800", "text": "STEP 2. The gamma-chart at (5,20) is a FAMILY: phi_gamma(x)=x y^gamma, phi_gamma(y)=y^-delta with gamma+delta = D = deg(P_1)/m = deg(Q_1)/n = 5 and gcd(gamma,delta)=1, so gamma in {1,2,3,4}. Derivation: (a1)/(b1) force P = C^2 with C monic in x, so the max-x vertex of N(P_1) must map to a pure power of x, giving apex = m*(delta,gamma) with gcd(gamma,delta)=1; deg(P_1)=m*D puts that apex on the total-degree face. GGV3's two published charts are the gamma=3 and gamma=2 members. gamma_chart.py reproduces 30/30 published data points of (a1)-(a6) and (b1)-(b6) from this law alone."}
