{"cite": "GGV3 tex:1735-1745 calls phi_3 an automorphism of K[x,y,y^-1]; det = -2 says otherwise", "drops": ["membership in the image of phi_3, i.e. the parity congruence J = I (mod 2) on every window coefficient", "the reduced polygon's shape beyond its two supporting faces"], "dst": "GCHART_G3", "ev": "edge", "id": "GE7", "map_kind": "RATIONAL", "src": "REDUCED_5_20", "type": "NECESSARY_CONDITION", "why": "phi_3 is an injective ENDOMORPHISM, not an automorphism: its exponent matrix has determinant -2, so it is a 2-fold cover of the torus. Its image lies in the sublattice {y-exponent = 3*(x-exponent) mod 2}. GGV3's (a1)-(a6), stated abstractly, do NOT carry that congruence, so the step from the reduced pair to the (a1)-(a6) model forgets it.", "witness": "the dropped congruence is visible in the published data it silently satisfies: (a6) C_0 has only EVEN y-exponents and (a3) F_{-1} = y^7 only odd. Nothing in (a1)-(a6) states this; the chart map implies it."}
{"cite": "GGV3 tex:1778-1782", "drops": ["membership in the image of phi_2, i.e. the congruence J = 2I (mod 3)", "the reduced polygon's shape beyond its two supporting faces"], "dst": "GCHART_G2", "ev": "edge", "id": "GE8", "map_kind": "RATIONAL", "src": "REDUCED_5_20", "type": "NECESSARY_CONDITION", "why": "Same as GE7 with delta = 3: phi_2 has determinant -3, a 3-fold cover, and (b1)-(b6) do not carry the resulting congruence J = 2I (mod 3).", "witness": "(b5) C_{-1} has exponents 1,-2,-5,...,-20 and (b6) C_1 has -1,-4,-7,-10: both exactly the congruence classes phi_2 permits, neither stated as a condition."}
{"cite": "gamma_chart.py: the chart law is validated 30/30 on its gamma=3 and gamma=2 instances; gamma=4 is the third member of the same one-parameter family", "drops": ["the reduced polygon's shape beyond its two supporting faces"], "dst": "GCHART_G4", "ev": "edge", "id": "GE9", "map_kind": "POLYNOMIAL", "src": "REDUCED_5_20", "type": "NECESSARY_CONDITION", "why": "phi_4 has determinant -1 and is a genuine automorphism, so the covering loss of GE7/GE8 is ABSENT here -- there is no congruence to drop. What is still dropped is the reduced polygon's shape: the target model retains only the chart map and the two supporting faces it transports.", "witness": "delta = 1 means phi_4 imposes no congruence at all, so the gamma=4 window ledger is strictly DENSER than gamma=2 or gamma=3 -- every y-exponent is legal in every slot. A kill argument that leans on a congruence at gamma=2,3 has nothing to lean on here."}
