{"debt_why": "The cap slope alpha is the slope of the face of N(P_1) COMPLEMENTARY to the total-degree face. The total-degree face is chart-independent (it gives the depth floor J >= 5(I-delta), verified 3/3), but the complementary face is not: it is fixed by the reduced polygon Delta'_gamma, and Delta'_gamma is not known for gamma=4. Two published values of alpha -- 1 at gamma=3 and 1/4 at gamma=2 -- do not determine a third; infinitely many laws in gamma fit both, and choosing one would be a guess dressed as a derivation. WHAT WOULD CLOSE IT: Delta'_4, which needs the EDGE ROOT SHIFT branch that polygon_reduction.case_f2 does not enumerate. Its pre-inversion upper edge (0,1)--(20,5) carries lattice points (5t,1+t), t=0..4, which the inversion (i,j)->(4j-i,j) sends to (4-t,1+t) = (delta,gamma) for gamma = t+1; t is exactly GGHV22's phi3 edge-root-shift depth, which case_8_28() performs (t=6, (0,1)->(24,7)) and case_f2() does not.", "dst": "GCHART_G4_LEDGER", "ev": "edge", "id": "GE10", "src": "GCHART_G4", "type": "UNTYPED", "why": "Nothing derived here fixes the gamma=4 degree cap."}
