{"cite": "1406.0886_GGV3.tex:1858-1875 -- the elimination is GGV3's, quoted, NOT independently recomputed here. Typing the step and trusting its arithmetic are separate questions; this field answers the first.", "desc": "GGV3 sec.5's gamma=3 window system AFTER eliminating the deep unknowns C_{-3}..C_{-7}: the relation C_0(3 C_0 C_{-1}^2 - 3 C_{-2}^2 - 2 lambda) = 2 C_0 F_{-2} (tex:1871), instantiated with (a5)'s consequences C_{-1}=a y^3, C_{-2}=b y^4, with C_0 the (a6) window c_{0,2}y^2..c_{0,-10}y^-10 and F_{-2} = f8 y^8+f6 y^6+f4 y^4+f2 y^2. Variables m_k = c_{0,-k}, L = lambda; the whole identity is cleared by y^14 and rewritten in u = y^2, one generator per coefficient of u^0..u^12. The last two generators are Rabinowitsch: 1-z*m10 asserts (a6)'s c_{0,-10} != 0, and 1-w*a asserts a in K^* -- which is exactly what (a5) buys, since deg_y(C_{-1}) <= 3 together with y^7 = -3 C_{-1}C_{-2} forces C_{-1} to be the MONOMIAL a y^3 with a invertible. Without a != 0 the system is satisfiable.", "ev": "model", "id": "G3_ELIM_KILL"}
{"cite": "1406.0886_GGV3.tex:1858-1875 -- the elimination is GGV3's, quoted, NOT independently recomputed here. Typing the step and trusting its arithmetic are separate questions; this field answers the first.", "drops": ["the deep window unknowns C_{-3}..C_{-7} and, with them, the liftability of any solution found downstairs", "the boundary of the image: what is returned is the closure, so points on the closure's edge may have no preimage"], "dst": "G3_ELIM_KILL", "ev": "edge", "id": "E-G3_ELIM_KILL", "map_kind": "POLYNOMIAL", "src": "GCHART_G3", "type": "IMAGE_CLOSURE", "why": "This step ELIMINATES the deep window unknowns C_{-3}, C_{-4}, C_{-5}, C_{-6}, C_{-7} from E_2=..=E_5=0, E_6=-F_{-1}, E_7=-F_{-2}. What comes back is the Zariski closure of the projection, so a point of the target need not lift to a full window solution: solvability does NOT transport forward. Emptiness does transport backward, which is the direction this computation is used in.", "witness": "The eliminated relation mentions neither C_{-3} nor F_{-1}, both of which are constrained upstream (F_{-1} = -3C_{-1}C_{-2} = y^7). A solution of the eliminated relation carries no obligation to satisfy that, so the target is strictly looser."}
{"certificate": "UNIT_IDEAL_CERT", "cite": "cas_ideal_is_unit, Singular via WSL, characteristic 0: std(I) = 1 on the 13 coefficient generators of C_0(3 a^2 C_0 y^6 - 3 b^2 y^8 - 2 lambda - 2 F_{-2}) = 0 plus the two Rabinowitsch generators. This is a MECHANISED replay of GGV3 tex:1875-1878 ('which contradicts that by (a6) we have c_{0,-10} != 0. This rules out the case gamma=3'), and it is the first time that half of the (50,75) argument has been machine-checked here -- F2_TOWER's a2_certificate() covers the gamma=2 half only.", "ev": "claim", "id": "GC-G3-KILL", "kind": "EMPTY", "ladder": "exact-checked", "model": "G3_ELIM_KILL", "statement": "the gamma=3 window system at (50,75) has no solution with c_{0,-10} != 0 and a in K^*"}
{"asserted": "the gamma=3 chart is killed at (50,75), and the kill lifts back to the reduced pair (P_1,Q_1)", "cite": "Both hops are read AGAINST the arrow, which is the licensed direction for EMPTY: IMAGE_CLOSURE/AGAINST/EMPTY = yes (an elimination cannot create solutions, so emptiness downstairs is emptiness upstairs), and NECESSARY_CONDITION/AGAINST/EMPTY = yes (the chart model is the relaxation; emptiness of the relaxation is emptiness of the source).", "claim": "GC-G3-KILL", "era": "live-2026-07", "ev": "inference", "id": "GI-G3-KILL-LIFTS", "note": "POSITIVE CONTROL for Step 2, and a direction test. The naive reading -- 'I eliminated variables and got a contradiction, so the contradiction propagates forward' -- is the ALONG direction, and IMAGE_CLOSURE/ALONG/EMPTY is NO. Getting this backwards is how an elimination-based kill becomes unsound. Note also what is NOT claimed: nothing here transports to (75,125). That is GE4, still UNTYPED.", "path": [["E-G3_ELIM_KILL", "AGAINST"], ["GE7", "AGAINST"]]}
{"domain": "gamma_window", "ev": "note", "source": "portage-depot/gamma_chart.py, STEP2_GAMMA_CHART.md", "text": "STEP 2 RESULT. (a5) deg_y(C_{-k}) <= k+2 is DERIVED for gamma=3 as the supporting face J <= delta - I of the reduced polygon pushed through phi_gamma, with the complementary face J >= D(I-delta) giving (a6)'s floor c_{0,-10}; the fitted cap slope alpha=1 is tight on all five published tops. For gamma=2 the same construction gives alpha=1/4 and reproduces (b3),(b4),(b5),(b6). For gamma=4 the CHART EXISTS (x|->x y^4, y|->y^-1, the unique automorphism in the family) and L1-L4 are derived, but the cap alpha is NOT -- see GE10. Two further results fell out: (i) phi_2 and phi_3 are ramified covers, not automorphisms, and their image congruences J = gamma*I (mod delta) account for every unexplained exponent pattern in (a3),(a6),(b5),(b6); (ii) polygon_reduction.case_f2(0)'s Delta' is the gamma=1 member of the family, and gamma=1 is excluded by GGV1 condition (8) -- so Delta' is not the polygon GGV3's charts act on, and gamma is precisely the edge-root-shift depth t+1 that case_f2's branch manifest omits."}
{"cite": "GGV3 tex:1866-1869 states a,b in K^* as a CONSEQUENCE of (a5) plus F_{-1} = y^7; this model is that consequence withheld.", "desc": "NEGATIVE CONTROL. The same eliminated gamma=3 system as G3_ELIM_KILL, with the single generator 1-w*a REMOVED -- i.e. with the invertibility of a dropped. a in K^* is exactly what (a5) buys: deg_y(C_{-1}) <= 3 together with F_{-1} = y^7 = -3 C_{-1}C_{-2} forces C_{-1} to be the MONOMIAL a*y^3 with a a unit, because y^7 is a monomial and the units of K[y,y^-1] are the monomials. If this ideal is NOT the unit ideal, then (a5) is load-bearing in the (50,75) gamma=3 kill rather than decorative -- which is the whole point of deriving it.", "ev": "model", "id": "G3_ELIM_NO_A5"}
{"cite": "GGV3 tex:1866-1869 states a,b in K^* as a CONSEQUENCE of (a5) plus F_{-1} = y^7; this model is that consequence withheld.", "drops": ["a != 0, i.e. the invertibility of C_{-1}'s leading coefficient", "with it, the whole contribution of (a5) to the gamma=3 kill"], "dst": "G3_ELIM_NO_A5", "ev": "edge", "id": "E-G3_ELIM_NO_A5", "map_kind": "IDENTITY_MAP", "src": "G3_ELIM_KILL", "type": "NECESSARY_CONDITION", "why": "Dropping the generator 1-w*a discards the requirement a != 0. Every point of the source is a point of the target and not conversely, so the target is a strict relaxation. Concretely it discards what (a5) contributes to the argument.", "witness": "a = 0 is a point of the target: with a = 0 the quadratic term 3a^2 S^2 vanishes and the system degenerates to S*T = 0, which S != 0, T = 0 satisfies with m10 != 0. It is not a point of the source."}
{"cite": "cas_ideal_is_unit, char 0: std(I) does NOT reduce to (1) (leading basis element f6). Independently, an explicit K-point: a = b = lambda = f2 = f4 = f6 = f8 = c_{0,2} = c_{0,0} = c_{0,-2} = c_{0,-4} = c_{0,-6} = c_{0,-8} = 0, c_{0,-10} = 1, z = 1. At a = 0 the quadratic term 3a^2 S^2 drops out and the identity degenerates to S*T = 0, satisfied by T = 0 with S != 0. All 14 generators vanish; verified by substitution.", "ev": "claim", "id": "GC-A5-LOAD-BEARING", "kind": "NONEMPTY", "ladder": "exact-checked", "model": "G3_ELIM_NO_A5", "statement": "with a != 0 withheld, the eliminated gamma=3 system has a solution with c_{0,-10} != 0"}
{"domain": "gamma_window", "ev": "note", "source": "portage-depot/gamma_chart.py sec.7; models G3_ELIM_KILL and G3_ELIM_NO_A5", "text": "NEGATIVE CONTROL, and the point of Step 2. G3_ELIM_KILL is EMPTY (std = 1); G3_ELIM_NO_A5 -- the same system with only `a != 0` withheld -- is NONEMPTY with an exhibited point. So (a5) is LOAD-BEARING in GGV3's gamma=3 kill, not decorative: it is what forces C_{-1} to be the monomial a*y^3 with a a unit, and without that unit the contradiction does not close. Deriving (a5) from the chart map therefore derives a step the kill actually stands on. NO INFERENCE IS RECORDED FROM THIS CLAIM, deliberately: NONEMPTY does not travel AGAINST a NECESSARY_CONDITION edge (the transport table says NO), so the witness at G3_ELIM_NO_A5 says nothing about G3_ELIM_KILL and must not be read as weakening the kill. It is a statement about which hypotheses the PROOF needs, not about the geometry of the source."}
